    "durationMs": 69342,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully tested. I built it on Express 5.3.0 with `pg` as the persistence layer:\n\n- **`start.sh`** — applies pending migrations via `scripts/migrate.js` (tracked in a `schema_migrations` table, idempotent), then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`. Deps were installed now, not in the script.\n- **`src/app.js`** — all routes: `POST /links` (201 with `{code, url, clicks: 0}`, URL returned unchanged, auto-generated 8-char codes, 409 on duplicate custom code), `GET /links/:code`, `GET /r/:code` (atomic `clicks = clicks + 1` in the same UPDATE that returns the URL, then 302), and `GET /links` (ascending creation order, `{items, total}`). Validation covers the 4–20 char `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` code pattern and absolute http/https URLs with a host; malformed JSON, bad URLs, and bad codes all return 422 JSON.\n- **`src/db.js`** — pg pool reading `DATABASE_URL`, nothing hard-coded.\n\nI verified every requirement with a curl suite: all status codes, code-length boundaries (20 passes, 21 fails), click increments across multiple redirects, and a full server restart confirming both data and click counts persist. The dev server is stopped and the port is free for the graded run."
  }
